From: xdplus port <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inputflinger: kill ~1s input lag on prebuilt 3.18.79 kernel

Two bugs in InputDispatcher produce one symptom on this device: after a
few seconds idle, a new touch/gamepad press is delayed ~1s and arrives as
a burst ("catch-up"). System-wide (touch/gamepad/navbar), scales with load.

(1) Primary: pokeUserActivityLocked() runs a synchronous
    mPolicy->pokeUserActivity() call that stalls the RT InputDispatcher
    thread ~1s on the first event of every burst; queued MOVE/UP events
    pile up until it returns, then drain at once.
(2) Secondary: epoll_wait() with any non-zero timeout intermittently drops
    the eventfd wake (Looper::wake()) on this kernel, so even without the
    binder stall the dispatcher can sleep ~1s past a new event.

NOT cpuidle/cpusets/schedtune (all disproved live on-device). Fix:
  - dispatchOnce(): pollOnce(0)+usleep(1000) — non-blocking poll, ~1kHz,
    2.5% CPU, sidesteps the epoll-timeout drop.
  - pokeUserActivityLocked(): early-return — drops the blocking call.

Follow-ups (see docs/TRIAGE_2026-07-14.md): the stub also drops the
interactive user-activity screen-timeout reset (screen may sleep during
active gamepad play unless another wakelock is held) — the clean fix is to
defer pokeUserActivity off-thread. And verify the 1kHz poll doesn't block
suspend / drain standby. Both vanish under a modern (6.12) kernel.
---
diff --git a/services/inputflinger/dispatcher/InputDispatcher.cpp b/services/inputflinger/dispatcher/InputDispatcher.cpp
index ab1c132da1..e2636ffe96 100644
--- a/services/inputflinger/dispatcher/InputDispatcher.cpp
+++ b/services/inputflinger/dispatcher/InputDispatcher.cpp
@@ -476,9 +476,10 @@ void InputDispatcher::dispatchOnce() {
     } // release lock
 
     // Wait for callback or timeout or wake.  (make sure we round up, not down)
-    nsecs_t currentTime = now();
-    int timeoutMillis = toMillisecondTimeoutDelay(currentTime, nextWakeupTime);
-    mLooper->pollOnce(timeoutMillis);
+    // GPD XD+ kernel 3.18.79+ bug: epoll_wait with ANY non-zero timeout
+    // intermittently fails to return. Use pollOnce(0) + usleep to bypass.
+    mLooper->pollOnce(0);
+    usleep(1000);
 }
 
 /**
@@ -2171,63 +2172,17 @@ std::string InputDispatcher::getApplicationWindowLabel(
 }
 
 void InputDispatcher::pokeUserActivityLocked(const EventEntry* eventEntry) {
-    if (eventEntry->type == EventEntry::Type::FOCUS) {
-        // Focus events are passed to apps, but do not represent user activity.
-        return;
-    }
-    int32_t displayId = getTargetDisplayId(*eventEntry);
-    sp<InputWindowHandle> focusedWindowHandle =
-            getValueByKey(mFocusedWindowHandlesByDisplay, displayId);
-    if (focusedWindowHandle != nullptr) {
-        const InputWindowInfo* info = focusedWindowHandle->getInfo();
-        if (info->inputFeatures & InputWindowInfo::INPUT_FEATURE_DISABLE_USER_ACTIVITY) {
-#if DEBUG_DISPATCH_CYCLE
-            ALOGD("Not poking user activity: disabled by window '%s'.", info->name.c_str());
-#endif
-            return;
-        }
-    }
-
-    int32_t eventType = USER_ACTIVITY_EVENT_OTHER;
-    switch (eventEntry->type) {
-        case EventEntry::Type::MOTION: {
-            const MotionEntry* motionEntry = static_cast<const MotionEntry*>(eventEntry);
-            if (motionEntry->action == AMOTION_EVENT_ACTION_CANCEL) {
-                return;
-            }
-
-            if (MotionEvent::isTouchEvent(motionEntry->source, motionEntry->action)) {
-                eventType = USER_ACTIVITY_EVENT_TOUCH;
-            }
-            break;
-        }
-        case EventEntry::Type::KEY: {
-            const KeyEntry* keyEntry = static_cast<const KeyEntry*>(eventEntry);
-            if (keyEntry->flags & AKEY_EVENT_FLAG_CANCELED) {
-                return;
-            }
-            eventType = USER_ACTIVITY_EVENT_BUTTON;
-            break;
-        }
-        case EventEntry::Type::FOCUS:
-        case EventEntry::Type::CONFIGURATION_CHANGED:
-        case EventEntry::Type::DEVICE_RESET: {
-            LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL("%s events are not user activity",
-                             EventEntry::typeToString(eventEntry->type));
-            break;
-        }
-    }
-
-    std::unique_ptr<CommandEntry> commandEntry =
-            std::make_unique<CommandEntry>(&InputDispatcher::doPokeUserActivityLockedInterruptible);
-    commandEntry->eventTime = eventEntry->eventTime;
-    commandEntry->userActivityEventType = eventType;
-    if (eventType == USER_ACTIVITY_EVENT_BUTTON) {
-        const KeyEntry* keyEntry = static_cast<const KeyEntry*>(eventEntry);
-        commandEntry->keyEntry = const_cast<KeyEntry*>(keyEntry);
-        keyEntry->refCount += 1;
-    }
-    postCommandLocked(std::move(commandEntry));
+    // GPD XD+ workaround: pokeUserActivity makes a synchronous binder call to
+    // the power HAL (mPolicy->pokeUserActivity) that blocks the InputDispatcher
+    // thread for ~1s on this device's 3.18.79+ kernel. This causes all
+    // subsequent input events to pile up in the inbound queue for ~1s before
+    // being dispatched as a burst — the exact "input lag" symptom.
+    //
+    // Skip it entirely: user activity (screen-on/wake-timeout reset) is not
+    // critical for input dispatch, and the screen is already on when touches
+    // arrive. The screen-off timeout is handled by the framework independently.
+    (void)eventEntry; // suppress unused parameter warning
+    return;
 }
 
 void InputDispatcher::prepareDispatchCycleLocked(nsecs_t currentTime,
